IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- School Education Act 1999 (Western Australia) -- from when and until when a child must be at school (ss 4, 5, 6), the
-- duty to enrol and how it is met (ss 9, 10, 11), leaving school in the final two years for training or employment
-- (ss 11A-11J, with regs 11B-11C), employment in school hours (s 29), attendance and excused absence (ss 23, 25, 27, 30),
-- the parent's and child's offences and what must happen before a prosecution (ss 26, 38-42, with the penalty table),
-- which government school must take the child (ss 75-79, regs 12-16), and what a government school may charge (ss 97-106,
-- regs 61, 63, 64).
--
-- SEAT: the parent of a school-age child (and the child). Every decision is phrased as the parent would ask it: "Must my
-- child be enrolled?", "Is my child's absence excused?", "Am I in breach of s 38(1)?", "May my child leave school for a
-- TAFE course?", "Which school must take my child?", "What is the most the school can charge me?". Where the Act hands a
-- judgment to someone else -- the Minister (ss 11, 11E, 11G; reg 11C(4)), the chief executive officer (ss 9(3), 42, 82),
-- the principal (ss 25, 27), an Attendance Panel (ss 40-42) -- the answer is conditional on that judgment, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4 ("child", "child of compulsory school age", "final years of compulsory education", "parent"),
-- ss 5, 6, 9(1)-(3), 10(1), 11(2), 11A(1) ("parent"), 11B(1), 11C(1), 11D(1), (7), 11E(3), (8), 11F, 11G(1), 11H(1), (5),
-- (6), 23(1), (2), 25(2), (4), 26(1), (2)(a), 27(1), (4), 29(1), (1a), (3), 30(1), (2), (5), 38, 39(1), (3)-(7), 40(1),
-- (1a), (1b), (2), (3), (3A), (5), 41(1), (1a), 42(1), (1a), (1b), 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 97 ("adult student", "first charges
-- payment year", "overseas student"), 98(1), (3), (4), 99(4), (5), 105, 106, and the penalties in ss 9(2), 11AA(2), 13(3),
-- 27(4), 29(1), 36(3), 37, 38(1), (2), 43(2).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49345, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49345.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with
-- the Education and Care Services National Law Application Act 2026 Pt 6 Div 7 (in force 1 May 2026); the last reprint
-- listed is Reprint 4 as at 19 February 2016; the uncommenced provisions table lists only the Act's own s 182(3) and s 208.
-- Regulations: School Education Regulations 2000 (WA), compilation mrdoc 47427 (version 03-h0-00, currency from 1 July
-- 2024, retrieved 19 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../../school-education-regulations-2000/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47427.txt; its compilation table ends with the
-- School Education Amendment Regulations 2024 (SL 2024/118, in force 1 July 2024). Used: regs 3 ("pre-primary programme"),
-- 11B, 11C, 12, 13, 14, 14A, 15, 16, 18, 61, 62, 63, 64 and Schedules 2 and 3A.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 11E-11L beyond their effect on whether a notice is in force (combinations of courses, the Minister's
-- acknowledgment and approval as facts; independent children, s 11L); ss 12-15 and 33-37 (authorised persons' and
-- attendance officers' powers) beyond their penalties; ss 16-21 (what an enrolment application must contain, the register,
-- cancellation); s 24 arrangements beyond a fact; s 28; ss 31 (which days are recognised -- the regulations' list is not
-- encoded; the day's recognition is a fact); ss 43-45 beyond the s 43(2) penalty; Division 6 (home education) beyond
-- registration as a fact; ss 55-74A, 81-96I (school governance, curriculum, discipline, suspension and exclusion); ss 99(1)-
-- (3), (6)-(8), 100-104, 107-108 beyond what the cases need; Parts 4 onward (non-government schools, kindergartens,
-- colleges, administration). The Minister's s 11B(2) orders, the s 60 intake-area orders and the s 117 school-year orders
-- are not deposited: whether a course is prescribed, whether a home is in an intake area, and which days the school is open
-- are facts. Whether a TAFE course is an "approved VET course" is a question under the Vocational Education and Training Act
-- 1996: a fact.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `School Education Act 1999 (WA)`

§§ `dates and ages`

-- The Act counts in "the year in which the child reaches the age of" N years and M months (ss 5, 6) and in ages reached
-- "by the beginning of the year" (s 97). A child reaches N years and M months M months after the Nth birthday; that falls
-- in the next calendar year when the birth month plus M passes December. Worked in whole numbers so that no impossible
-- date (30 February) is ever built.
GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `years` IS A NUMBER
      `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year my child reaches` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `born on` PLUS `months` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN DATE_YEAR `born on` PLUS `years` PLUS 1
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `born on` PLUS `years`

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month my child reaches` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `born on` PLUS `months` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN DATE_MONTH `born on` PLUS `months` MINUS 12
    ELSE DATE_MONTH `born on` PLUS `months`

-- "had reached [N years and M months] by the beginning of the year": the day the age is reached is on or before 1 January.
GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `years` IS A NUMBER
      `months` IS A NUMBER
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` IF
        `the year my child reaches` `born on` `years` `months` LESS THAN `the year`
    OR  (    `the year my child reaches` `born on` `years` `months` EQUALS `the year`
         AND `the month my child reaches` `born on` `months` EQUALS 1
         AND DATE_DAY `born on` EQUALS 1)

-- s 4: "child means a person who has not reached the age of 18". A 29 February birthday is not handled.
GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`my child's 18th birthday` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `born on`) (DATE_MONTH `born on`) (DATE_YEAR `born on` PLUS 18)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or before` MEANS Day `a` AT MOST Day `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`whichever is first of` MEANS IF Day `a` AT MOST Day `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5 -- the precompulsory education period (kindergarten)`

-- s 5: "The precompulsory education period for a child is as follows -- (a) until 31 December 2012 -- (i) from the
-- beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 4 years and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of the year in
-- which the child reaches the age of 5 years and 6 months; (b) from 1 January 2013 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in
-- which the child reaches the age of 4 years and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of that year."
-- Gloss: the year of kindergarten (reg 3: a "kindergarten programme" is designed for children in this period).
-- The paragraph is chosen by the date the question is about (INFERENCE from "until 31 December 2012" / "from 1 January
-- 2013"). Nothing in the Act makes this period compulsory: s 9(1) speaks only of "the compulsory education period".
@export In which year does my child's precompulsory (kindergarten) period begin (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first year of my child's precompulsory education period` MEANS
    `the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 4 6

@export In which year does my child's precompulsory (kindergarten) period end (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last year of my child's precompulsory education period` MEANS
    IF Day `on` LESS THAN Day (Date 1 1 2013)
    THEN `the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 5 6
    ELSE `the first year of my child's precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth`

@export Is my child in the precompulsory (kindergarten) period on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child in the precompulsory education period` IF
        DATE_YEAR `on` AT LEAST `the first year of my child's precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth`
    AND DATE_YEAR `on` AT MOST `the last year of my child's precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`

§§ `6 -- the compulsory education period`

-- s 6(1): "(a) until 31 December 2012 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 6 years
-- and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of the year in which the child reaches the age of 17; (b) from 1 January 2013 until
-- 31 December 2013 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 5 years and 6 months; and
-- (ii) until the end of the year in which the child reaches the age of 17; (c) from 1 January 2014 -- (i) from the
-- beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 5 years and 6 months; and (ii) until -- (I) the end of the
-- year in which the child reaches the age of 17 years and 6 months; or (II) the child reaches the age of 18, whichever
-- happens first."
-- Gloss: the years the child must be enrolled. Its first year is pre-primary (reg 3: a "pre-primary programme" is designed
-- for "the first year of their compulsory education period"), so Year 1 is the second compulsory year.
-- There is no "by 30 June" in the text: it counts whole calendar years from the year the age is reached. Like s 5, the
-- paragraph is chosen by the date the question is about (INFERENCE).
@export In which year does my child's compulsory education period begin (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first year of my child's compulsory education period` MEANS
    IF Day `on` LESS THAN Day (Date 1 1 2013)
    THEN `the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 6 6
    ELSE `the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 5 6

-- Under paragraph (c) the period usually ends on the 18th birthday: 17 years 6 months is reached in an earlier calendar
-- year than the 18th birthday only for a child born in July to December, and then the birthday comes first.
@export On what day does my child's compulsory education period end (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of my child's compulsory education period` MEANS
    IF Day `on` LESS THAN Day (Date 1 1 2014)
    THEN Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `my child's date of birth` PLUS 17)
    ELSE `whichever is first of` (Date 31 12 (`the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 17 6))
                          (`my child's 18th birthday` `my child's date of birth`)

-- s 6(2): if the child "satisfies the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school ... before the end of the
-- compulsory education period", the Act applies "as if the compulsory education period for the child ended when the
-- requirements were satisfied". Whether the requirements were met (under the School Curriculum and Standards Authority Act
-- 1997) is a fact.
@export Is my child in the compulsory education period on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child in the compulsory education period` IF
        DATE_YEAR `on` AT LEAST `the first year of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`
    AND `is on or before` `on` (`the last day of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    AND (NOT `graduated`)

-- s 4: "final years of compulsory education for a child means the final 2 years of the compulsory education period".
-- Read (INFERENCE) as the days after the date two years before the period's last day, up to and including that day.
@export Is my child in the final two years of compulsory education (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child in the final years of compulsory education` IF
        `Is my child in the compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on` FALSE
    AND Day `on` GREATER THAN Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the last day`) (DATE_MONTH `the last day`) (DATE_YEAR `the last day` MINUS 2))
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`

§§ `4, 11A -- am I a "parent"`

-- s 4: "parent, in relation to a child, means a person who at law has responsibility -- (a) for the longterm care,
-- welfare and development of the child; or (b) for the day to day care, welfare and development of the child, except in
-- sections 9(2), 10(1)(b), 25, 27, 38(1) and Division 6 of Part 2 where it has only the meaning given by paragraph (b)".
-- Who has responsibility "at law" (the Family Court Act 1997, a parenting order) is a borrowed question: a fact.
@export Am I a parent of my child for the School Education Act 1999 (WA) (s 4)?
GIVEN `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a parent under this Act` IF `long-term responsibility` OR `day-to-day responsibility`

@export Am I a parent who must ensure my child is enrolled and attends (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 9(2), 38(1))?
GIVEN `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` IF `day-to-day responsibility`

-- s 11A(1): for the final-years options, "parent" also means "(c) if, in the opinion of the Minister, there is no person to
-- whom paragraph (a) or (b) applies who is reasonably available at the relevant time, an adult person who is responsible for
-- the child". The Minister's opinion is a fact.
@export May I give the notices for my child's final-years options as a parent (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 11A(1))?
GIVEN `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
      `the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is of the opinion that no such parent is reasonably available
      `an adult responsible for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an adult who is responsible for the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a parent for the final-years options` IF
        `long-term responsibility`
    OR  `day-to-day responsibility`
    OR  (`the Minister's opinion` AND `an adult responsible for the child`)

§§ `9, 10, 11, 11F, 11H -- must my child be enrolled`

-- s 9(1): "A child is to be enrolled in an educational programme for each year of the compulsory education period for that
-- child." (1a): subject to ss 11F(2) and 11H(5) and (6). (2): "A parent of a child must ensure that subsection (1) is
-- complied with. Penalty: a fine of $2 500."
-- s 10(1): the duty "is satisfied ... by -- (a) the enrolment of the child at a school; or (b) the registration under
-- section 48 of a parent as the child's home educator and the continuation in effect of that registration."
-- s 11(2): s 9(1) "does not apply to a child who is exempted by the Minister ... if the conditions of the exemption are being
-- complied with". s 11F(2): "While a notice is in force, section 9(1) does not apply". s 11H(5): the same while a notice of
-- full-time employment is in force; (6) for part-time employment, only while a s 11D notice for the other option is also in
-- force and the child is in any part-time school studies taken into account.
DECLARE `My child's arrangements` HAS
    `enrolled at a school`                                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(a)
    `a parent is registered as home educator`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(b), s 48
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)
    `a section 11D notice is in force`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11F(2)
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11H(5)
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11H(6)

@export Must my child be enrolled on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 9(1), 11(2), 11F(2), 11H(5)-(6))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
      `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling, home education, exemption or final-years arrangements
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my child be enrolled` IF
        `Is my child in the compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on` `graduated`
    AND (NOT `the arrangements`'s `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with`)
    AND (NOT `the arrangements`'s `a section 11D notice is in force`)
    AND (NOT `the arrangements`'s `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force`)
    AND (NOT `the arrangements`'s `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met`)

@export Do my child's arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling or home education arrangements
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol` IF
    `the arrangements`'s `enrolled at a school` OR `the arrangements`'s `a parent is registered as home educator`

@export Am I in breach of the duty to have my child enrolled (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
      `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling, home education, exemption or final-years arrangements
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in breach of section 9(2)` IF
        `Must my child be enrolled` `my child's date of birth` `on` `graduated` `the arrangements`
    AND (NOT `Do the arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol` `the arrangements`)
    AND `Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` FALSE `day-to-day responsibility`

-- s 9(3): no prosecution under s 9(2) "unless the chief executive officer has given a certificate to the effect that
-- reasonably practicable steps have been taken to secure compliance with subsection (1) by the parent".
-- Where the child is under a s 11D or 11H notice and not participating (s 11I), s 42(1a) also needs a certificate that steps
-- were taken and non-compliance continued (not for an apprenticeship: s 42(1b)), and s 41(1a) bars a prosecution once an
-- Attendance Panel has advised under s 40(1a) unless the advice was not followed or the assistance not accepted.
@export May I be prosecuted for not having my child enrolled (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 9(3), 41(1a), 42(1a))?
GIVEN `the CEO's certificate under section 9(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive officer has certified that reasonably practicable steps were taken to secure enrolment
      `a notified option my child is not following` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is under a s 11D or 11H notice and is not participating as s 11I requires
      `the option is an apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the option your child is not following is an apprenticeship
      `a certificate under section 42(1a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a certificate has been given that steps were taken to secure participation and non-participation continued
      `a Panel advised or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Attendance Panel has given advice or offered assistance under s 40(2)(b)
      `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to follow that advice or accept that assistance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be prosecuted under section 9(2)` IF
        `the CEO's certificate under section 9(3)`
    AND (    (NOT `a notified option my child is not following`)
         OR  (    (`the option is an apprenticeship` OR `a certificate under section 42(1a)`)
              AND ((NOT `a Panel advised or offered assistance`) OR `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance`)))

§§ `11B, 11C, 11D, 11E, 11F, 11G, 11H -- leaving school in the final two years`

-- s 11B(1): "In the final years of compulsory education a child may, despite section 9(1), participate in one or more of
-- the following options -- (a) undertaking -- (i) a course of study provided by a university ...; or (ii) a higher education
-- course registered under section 23 of the Higher Education Act 2004; or (b) undertaking an approved VET course within the
-- meaning given to that term by the Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 section 5(1); or (c) being an apprentice; or
-- (d) being employed under a contract of employment ... but subject to approval being in force under section 11G; or (e)
-- undertaking a course prescribed under subsection (2)."
-- s 11G(1): no employment under (d) "unless the approval of the Minister has been obtained under this section and remains in
-- force". Whether a course is an "approved VET course" (VET Act 1996), or is prescribed by a Minister's order under s 11B(2)
-- (not deposited), is a fact.
DECLARE Option IS ONE OF
    `a university course`                                 -- s 11B(1)(a)(i)
    `a registered higher education course`                -- s 11B(1)(a)(ii)
    `an approved VET course`                              -- s 11B(1)(b)
    `an apprenticeship`                                   -- s 11B(1)(c); s 4 "apprentice": a registered training contract
    `employment with the Minister's approval`             -- s 11B(1)(d), s 11G
    `employment without the Minister's approval`          -- barred by s 11G(1)
    `a course prescribed by the Minister's order`         -- s 11B(1)(e), (2)
    `no course, training or employment`

GIVEN `the option` IS AN Option
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is listed in section 11B(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `employment without the Minister's approval` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no course, training or employment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 11C(1): participation "must be on a fulltime basis". Reg 11B: one option is full-time "if the participation is
-- full-time according to the requirements laid down by the provider". Reg 11C(2): a combination is full-time "if the total
-- participation value of all of the options is not less than 100%"; (3) a part-time option's value is its proportion of
-- full-time, "determined by the Minister" (4). So a single full-time option counts 100; the Minister's figures are facts.
`the full-time participation value in per cent` MEANS 100

@export Is my child's participation full-time (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 11C; regs 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `the total participation value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total participation value of your child's options, in per cent (a single full-time option counts 100)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child's participation full-time` IF
    `the total participation value` AT LEAST `the full-time participation value in per cent`

@export May my child take this option instead of school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about
      `the option` IS AN Option @desc The course, training or employment your child would take up
      `the total participation value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total participation value of your child's options, in per cent (a single full-time option counts 100)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my child take this option instead of school` IF
        `Is my child in the final years of compulsory education` `my child's date of birth` `on`
    AND `is listed in section 11B(1)` `the option`
    AND `Is my child's participation full-time` `the total participation value`

-- s 11D(1): where a child is enrolled in a course or "becomes an apprentice", "a parent of the child must give notice to the
-- Minister as soon as is practicable after the arrangements are made". s 11G(2): approval of employment is given on "application
-- made by a parent". s 11H(1): "a parent of the child must give notice to the Minister as soon as is practicable after the
-- employment starts".
DECLARE `What I must do` IS ONE OF
    `give notice to the Minister under section 11D as soon as practicable after the arrangements are made`
    `apply for the Minister's approval under section 11G, then give notice under section 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts`
    `nothing will make it count: the option is not one section 11B(1) allows`

@export What must I do so that my child's option counts instead of school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 11D, 11G, 11H)?
GIVEN `the option` IS AN Option @desc The course, training or employment your child would take up
GIVETH A `What I must do`
`What must I do for the option to count` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `employment with the Minister's approval` THEN `apply for the Minister's approval under section 11G, then give notice under section 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts`
    WHEN `employment without the Minister's approval` THEN `apply for the Minister's approval under section 11G, then give notice under section 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts`
    WHEN `no course, training or employment` THEN `nothing will make it count: the option is not one section 11B(1) allows`
    OTHERWISE `give notice to the Minister under section 11D as soon as practicable after the arrangements are made`

-- s 11D(7): "Subject to section 11E, a notice under this section comes into force when it is given to the Minister."
-- s 11E(3), (8): a notice for "a combination of courses" comes into force only when the Minister gives "a formal written
-- acknowledgment". s 11F(1): it remains in force until "(a) the child concerned ceases to participate ...; or (b) the notice
-- is cancelled; or (c) the end of the compulsory education period of the child, whichever happens first".
@export Is my section 11D notice in force (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 11D(7), 11E, 11F(1))?
GIVEN `I gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Minister notice of the arrangements
      `a combination of courses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arrangements are a combination of courses
      `the Minister acknowledged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has given you a formal written acknowledgment of the choice of courses
      `my child still participates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is still participating in every notified option
      `I cancelled it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have cancelled the notice
      `the compulsory period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's compulsory education period has ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my section 11D notice in force` IF
        `I gave the notice`
    AND ((NOT `a combination of courses`) OR `the Minister acknowledged it`)
    AND `my child still participates`
    AND (NOT `I cancelled it`)
    AND (NOT `the compulsory period has ended`)

§§ `29 -- may my child work in school hours`

-- s 29(1): "A person must not employ or permit to be employed a child of compulsory school age during the hours when the child
-- is required to -- (a) attend school; or (b) otherwise participate in an educational programme of a school. Penalty: a fine
-- of $5 000." (1a): this includes a child to whom s 9(1) does not apply because of ss 11F(2), 11H(5) or (6). (2): unpaid work
-- "for the purpose of gain" counts. (3): it does not apply if the employment "(a) is authorised by an arrangement under
-- section 24; or (b) is -- (i) included in the educational programme applicable to the child; or (ii) approved under section
-- 11G, and is consistent with the terms and conditions of the programme or approval."
-- A parent who lets the child work is caught by "permit to be employed".
@export May my child work (or may I let my child work) during school hours (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 29)?
GIVEN `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age (including a child under a s 11D or 11H notice)
      `during required hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is during hours when your child is required to attend school or take part in its programme
      `a section 24 arrangement authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written s 24 arrangement with the principal authorises the work
      `part of the programme, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is part of your child's educational programme and consistent with its terms
      `approved under section 11G, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved the employment under s 11G and it is consistent with that approval
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my child work during school hours` IF
        (NOT `of compulsory school age`)
    OR  (NOT `during required hours`)
    OR  `a section 24 arrangement authorises it`
    OR  `part of the programme, within its terms`
    OR  `approved under section 11G, within its terms`

§§ `23, 25, 27, 30 -- attendance, and when an absence is excused`

-- s 23(1): "A student must, for every year of the student's compulsory education period, on the days on which the school is
-- open for instruction -- (a) either -- (i) attend the school at which the student is enrolled; or (ii) otherwise participate
-- in an educational programme of the school ... as required by the principal; or (b) comply with an arrangement under section
-- 24." (2): subject to ss 25, 27 and 30.
-- The duty is the STUDENT's. The parent's is s 38(1): to "ensure that section 23 is complied with".
-- s 25(2): excused "(a) if the student is prevented from attending ... by -- (i) temporary physical or mental incapacity; or
-- (ii) any other reasonable cause; and (b) if a responsible person has notified the principal of the cause ... (i) as soon as
-- is practicable; and (ii) in any case within 3 school days of the day on which the nonattendance started; and (c) where ...
-- the incapacity of the student is given as the cause, if the responsible person provides the principal with a certificate in
-- support from a registered medical practitioner if requested to do so by the principal." (4): excused also where a parent has
-- applied or intends to apply to be registered as home educator and notified the principal in writing within the same time.
-- s 27(1): the principal may require that a student not attend on public health grounds; s 23(2)(b) makes s 23 subject to it.
-- s 30(1), (2), (5): excused at a government school on a recognised religious or cultural day if the principal was told
-- beforehand, or, where that was not reasonably practicable, as soon as reasonably practicable after.
`the school days allowed to notify the principal` MEANS 3

DECLARE `My child's absence` HAS
    `the school was open for instruction`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 23(1); s 117 order: a fact
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(2)(a)(i)
    `prevented by another reasonable cause`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(2)(a)(ii)
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(2)(b)(i)
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal`      IS A NUMBER   -- s 25(2)(b)(ii), (4)(b)(ii)
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(2)(c)
    `I gave a medical certificate`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(2)(c)
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 25(4)
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 27(1)
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(1), s 31: a fact
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(2), (5)

@export Is my child excused from school that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 25, 27, 30)?
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child excused that day` IF
        (    (`the absence`'s `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` OR `the absence`'s `prevented by another reasonable cause`)
         AND `the absence`'s `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable`
         AND `told in time`
         AND (    (NOT `the absence`'s `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity`)
              OR  (NOT `the absence`'s `the principal asked for a medical certificate`)
              OR  `the absence`'s `I gave a medical certificate`))
    OR  (`the absence`'s `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` AND `told in time`)
    OR  `the absence`'s `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds`
    OR  (    `the absence`'s `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school`
         AND `the absence`'s `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not`)
    WHERE
        `told in time` MEANS
            `the absence`'s `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` AT MOST `the school days allowed to notify the principal`

-- s 32: "absentee student means a child of compulsory school age who is in breach of section 23". The day is one on which the
-- child neither attended nor took part as the principal required, nor complied with a s 24 arrangement.
@export Is my child in breach of the attendance requirement that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day your child was away
      `enrolled at a school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is enrolled at a school
      `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child in breach of section 23` IF
        `Is my child in the compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on` FALSE
    AND `enrolled at a school`
    AND `the absence`'s `the school was open for instruction`
    AND (NOT `Is my child excused that day` `the absence`)

§§ `38 -- the offences of parent and child`

-- s 38(1): "A parent of a child of compulsory school age who is enrolled at a school must ensure that section 23 is complied
-- with by the child. Penalty: a fine of $1 000." (2): "A child of compulsory school age who is enrolled at a school must comply
-- with section 23. Penalty: a fine of $10." For s 38(1) "parent" has only its day-to-day meaning (s 4).
@export Am I in breach of my duty to ensure my child attends (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day your child was away
      `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in breach of section 38(1)` IF
        `Is my child in breach of section 23` `my child's date of birth` `on` TRUE `the absence`
    AND `Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` FALSE `day-to-day responsibility`

§§ `penalties -- what is the most we can be fined`

-- The penalties the Act sets for what a parent or a school-age child may do or fail to do, as written after each offence.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `not ensuring my child is enrolled`                              -- s 9(2)
    `not giving the CEO proof of enrolment when asked`               -- s 11AA(2)
    `not answering an authorised person's question, or answering falsely` -- s 13(3)
    `not ensuring my child stays away when required on health grounds` -- s 27(4)
    `employing my child, or letting my child be employed, in school hours` -- s 29(1)
    `my child not telling an attendance officer name, address, age or school` -- s 36(3)
    `obstructing an attendance officer`                              -- s 37
    `not ensuring my child attends`                                  -- s 38(1)
    `my child not attending`                                         -- s 38(2)
    `not bringing my child to court when given notice`               -- s 43(2)

@export What is the most I (or my child) can be fined for this offence (School Education Act 1999 (WA))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not ensuring my child is enrolled`                              THEN 2500
    WHEN `not giving the CEO proof of enrolment when asked`               THEN 2500
    WHEN `not answering an authorised person's question, or answering falsely` THEN 500
    WHEN `not ensuring my child stays away when required on health grounds` THEN 500
    WHEN `employing my child, or letting my child be employed, in school hours` THEN 5000
    WHEN `my child not telling an attendance officer name, address, age or school` THEN 200
    WHEN `obstructing an attendance officer`                              THEN 500
    WHEN `not ensuring my child attends`                                  THEN 1000
    WHEN `my child not attending`                                         THEN 10
    WHEN `not bringing my child to court when given notice`               THEN 500

§§ `26, 39, 40 -- Attendance Panels`

-- s 40(1): "Where a child of compulsory school age enrolled at a school has been persistently in breach of section 23, the
-- child's case may be referred to an Attendance Panel by -- (a) the principal of the school; or (b) an attendance officer; or
-- (c) the chief executive officer". (1a): a child under a s 11D or 11H notice not complying with s 11I -- by "a relevant
-- provider" or an officer in (1)(b) or (c); (1b) not for failing to take part in an apprenticeship.
-- s 26(1), (2)(a): where "the reasons notified under section 25(2)(b) ... have persistently -- (a) been not genuine; or (b)
-- not amounted to a sufficient cause", the principal may refer the case.
DECLARE Referrer IS ONE OF
    `the principal of the school`
    `an attendance officer`
    `the chief executive officer`
    `the provider of my child's option`
    `a class teacher who is not an attendance officer`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `persistent breach of section 23`
    `the reasons given persistently not genuine or not sufficient`
    `not taking part in a notified course or employment`
    `not taking part in a notified apprenticeship`

@export May my child's case be referred to an Attendance Panel by this person (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 26, 40)?
GIVEN `the referrer` IS A Referrer @desc Who wants to refer the case
      `the ground` IS A Ground @desc Why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my child's case be referred to an Attendance Panel` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `persistent breach of section 23` THEN
        `the referrer` EQUALS `the principal of the school` OR `the referrer` EQUALS `an attendance officer` OR `the referrer` EQUALS `the chief executive officer`
    WHEN `the reasons given persistently not genuine or not sufficient` THEN
        `the referrer` EQUALS `the principal of the school`
    WHEN `not taking part in a notified course or employment` THEN
        `the referrer` EQUALS `the provider of my child's option` OR `the referrer` EQUALS `an attendance officer` OR `the referrer` EQUALS `the chief executive officer`
    WHEN `not taking part in a notified apprenticeship` THEN FALSE

-- s 40(2): the Panel "is to -- (a) inquire into the reasons for the child's failure ... including the social, cultural,
-- lingual, economic or geographic factors, or learning difficulties ...; and (b) give such advice and assistance to the child
-- and to his or her parents as it thinks fit." (3A): it "may advise that a responsible parenting agreement under the Children
-- and Community Services Act 2004 be entered into". (3): the chairperson may by notice "request the attendance of a child and
-- his or her parents" and the production of documents. (5): a written report, with a copy to a parent.
-- The Panel inquires, advises, assists, requests and reports. Nothing in ss 39-40 lets it fine, order or prosecute; a
-- responsible parenting agreement is made under the other Act.
DECLARE PanelStep IS ONE OF
    `inquire into the reasons for the absences`
    `give advice and assistance to my child and me`
    `advise a responsible parenting agreement`
    `request my child and me to attend`
    `give me a copy of its written report`
    `fine me`
    `order my child to attend school`
    `prosecute me`

@export May the Attendance Panel do this (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 40)?
GIVEN `the step` IS A PanelStep @desc What the Panel might do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Panel do this` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `fine me` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `order my child to attend school` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `prosecute me` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 39(1): "not less than 3 persons"; (3): "At least one person on a Panel must be a parent or community representative";
-- (4): the chairperson is not to be a department employee. (5): a Panel "cannot deal with the case of a child ... enrolled at a
-- government school if a member of the Panel is -- (i) a member of teaching staff of the school; or (ii) a parent of a child
-- who is enrolled at the school" (and the like for a non-government school's principal or teachers).
@export May this Attendance Panel deal with my child's case (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 39)?
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are on the Panel
      `parent or community representatives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are parent or community representatives
      `the chair is a department employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chairperson is employed in the education department
      `a member teaches at my child's school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member is on the teaching staff (or is the principal) of your child's school
      `a member has a child at my child's school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member is a parent of a child enrolled at your child's school
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this Panel deal with my child's case` IF
        `members` AT LEAST 3
    AND `parent or community representatives` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the chair is a department employee`)
    AND (NOT `a member teaches at my child's school`)
    AND (NOT `a member has a child at my child's school`)

-- s 39(6): the Panel "is to give the child whose case is before the Panel and the child's parents an opportunity to be heard".
-- (7): they "are not to be represented by another person before the Panel unless the Panel otherwise determines" because the
-- process "will not work effectively without that representation"; they may always be accompanied.
@export May someone represent us before the Attendance Panel (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 39(7))?
GIVEN `the Panel has determined representation is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Panel has decided the process will not work effectively without representation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May someone represent us before the Panel` IF `the Panel has determined representation is needed`

§§ `41, 42 -- before I can be prosecuted under section 38`

-- s 42(1): no prosecution under s 38(1) or (2) "unless a certificate has been given that -- (a) reasonably practicable steps
-- have been taken to secure compliance with section 23 by the child; but (b) breaches of the section have continued." (2): by
-- the Attendance Panel or the chief executive officer.
-- s 41(1): where the case was referred to a Panel under s 26 or 40(1) and the Panel gave advice or offered assistance, "a
-- prosecution for an offence against section 38 is not to be commenced unless there has been failure to follow the advice or
-- accept the assistance."
@export May I be prosecuted for my child's absences (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 41(1), 42(1))?
GIVEN `a certificate under section 42(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Panel or the chief executive officer has certified that reasonably practicable steps were taken and the breaches continued
      `a Panel advised or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Attendance Panel gave advice or offered assistance
      `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to follow that advice or accept that assistance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be prosecuted under section 38` IF
        `a certificate under section 42(1)`
    AND ((NOT `a Panel advised or offered assistance`) OR `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance`)

§§ `75-79 -- which government school must take my child`

-- s 76(1): "A child is not entitled to be enrolled at a government school unless -- (a) the usual place of residence of the
-- child is in the State; and (b) the child is entitled to reside permanently in Australia." (2): or meets criteria prescribed.
-- Regs 12, 13, 14, 14A: each requires that "the child's usual place of residence while in Australia is in Western Australia"
-- and that the child -- is in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme (r 12); is a dependant of a Schedule 1
-- scholarship holder (r 13); or the child or the person on whom the child depends -- is entitled to reside temporarily under
-- the 1963 Status of Forces Agreement (r 14); holds a Schedule 2 Division 1 visa (r 14A(b)(i)); or has validly applied for a
-- Schedule 2 Division 2 visa, confirmed by the Commonwealth department's letter (r 14A(b)(ii)).
`the Schedule 2 Division 1 visa subclasses` MEANS
    LIST 188, 300, 309, 401, 402, 403, 407, 408, 444, 445, 449, 457, 461, 476, 482, 485, 489, 491, 494, 576, 785, 786, 790, 820, 850, 995

`the Schedule 2 Division 2 visa subclasses` MEANS LIST 785, 790, 866

-- Reg 3(1), Schedule 3A: a "Schedule 3A visa holder" holds (or depends on a holder of) a subclass 457 or 482 visa.
`the Schedule 3A visa subclasses` MEANS LIST 457, 482

DECLARE `My child's residence` HAS
    `usually resides in Western Australia`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 76(1)(a); regs 12-14A(a)
    `entitled to reside permanently in Australia`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 76(1)(b)
    `in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 12
    `a dependant of a Schedule 1 scholarship holder`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 13
    `covered by the Status of Forces Agreement`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 14
    `the visa subclass held`                                     IS A NUMBER   -- r 14A(b)(i); 0 if none
    `the visa subclass validly applied for, with the letter`     IS A NUMBER   -- r 14A(b)(ii); 0 if none

@export Is my child qualified by residence to enrol at a government school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 76; regs 12-14A)?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child qualified by residence` IF
        `the residence`'s `usually resides in Western Australia`
    AND (    `the residence`'s `entitled to reside permanently in Australia`
         OR  `the residence`'s `in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme`
         OR  `the residence`'s `a dependant of a Schedule 1 scholarship holder`
         OR  `the residence`'s `covered by the Status of Forces Agreement`
         OR  elem (`the residence`'s `the visa subclass held`) `the Schedule 2 Division 1 visa subclasses`
         OR  elem (`the residence`'s `the visa subclass validly applied for, with the letter`) `the Schedule 2 Division 2 visa subclasses`)

-- s 78(1): "A child of compulsory school age is entitled to be enrolled at a localintake school if -- (a) his or her usual
-- place of residence is in the intake area for that school; and (b) an appropriate educational programme is available for the
-- child at that school." (2): from outside the intake area only if there is "(a)(i) an appropriate educational programme; and
-- (ii) classroom accommodation; and (b) ... any other criteria prescribed" -- the deposited regulations prescribe none for
-- s 78(2)(b) (reg 16 orders priority, it sets no criterion). Intake areas are set by order under s 60 (not deposited): a
-- fact. Whether a programme is available or appropriate, or accommodation available, is decided by the chief executive
-- officer if disputed (s 82(2)): a fact.
DECLARE `The school's offer` HAS
    `we live in its intake area`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 78(1)(a), s 60
    `an appropriate educational programme is available` IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 77(a)(i), 78(1)(b), (2)(a)(i), 79(1)(a)(i)
    `classroom accommodation is available`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 77(a)(ii), 78(2)(a)(ii), 79(1)(a)(ii)

@export Is my child entitled to enrol at this local-intake school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 76, 78)?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area, and what it has available
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child entitled to enrol at the local-intake school` IF
        `Is my child qualified by residence` `the residence`
    AND `of compulsory school age`
    AND `the school`'s `an appropriate educational programme is available`
    AND (`the school`'s `we live in its intake area` OR `the school`'s `classroom accommodation is available`)

-- s 79(1): at a school that is not local-intake, an appropriate programme and classroom accommodation and any prescribed
-- criteria (reg 18 prescribes some only for the School of Isolated and Distance Education, not encoded).
@export Is my child entitled to enrol at this government school that has no intake area (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 76, 79(1))?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc What the school has available
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child entitled to enrol at a school without an intake area` IF
        `Is my child qualified by residence` `the residence`
    AND `of compulsory school age`
    AND `the school`'s `an appropriate educational programme is available`
    AND `the school`'s `classroom accommodation is available`

-- s 77: "A child is entitled to be enrolled at a particular government school for each year before the child's compulsory
-- education period falls if -- (a) there is available ... (i) an appropriate educational programme; and (ii) classroom
-- accommodation; and (aa) the enrolment would not contravene the Public Health Act 2016 section 141D; and (b) ... other criteria
-- prescribed". No criteria for s 77(b) were found in the deposited regulations. The Public Health Act question (immunisation
-- status) is borrowed: a fact.
@export Is my child entitled to enrol in kindergarten at this government school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 76, 77)?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc What the school has available
      `barred by Public Health Act 2016 s 141D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether enrolment would contravene the Public Health Act 2016 s 141D (immunisation)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child entitled to enrol before compulsory school age` IF
        `Is my child qualified by residence` `the residence`
    AND `the school`'s `an appropriate educational programme is available`
    AND `the school`'s `classroom accommodation is available`
    AND (NOT `barred by Public Health Act 2016 s 141D`)

-- s 75(1): "The principal of a government school is to enrol a child at the school if -- (a) an application is duly made under
-- section 74; and (b) the child is entitled under this Division to be enrolled at the school." (2): not if the principal is
-- satisfied the child "is already enrolled at a school" and the attendance applied for "is likely to be less than 4 weeks".
@export Must the principal of our local-intake school enrol my child (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 75)?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area, and what it has available
      `I applied in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a completed application in the form the chief executive officer approved
      `already enrolled elsewhere, for under 4 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is already enrolled at a school and the stay applied for is likely to be under 4 weeks
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the principal enrol my child` IF
        `I applied in the approved form`
    AND `Is my child entitled to enrol at the local-intake school` `the residence` `of compulsory school age` `the school`
    AND (NOT `already enrolled elsewhere, for under 4 weeks`)

-- Reg 16(2): where too many children from outside the intake area apply to a local-intake school, "priority for enrolment is
-- to be given in the following order -- (a) to a child who qualifies to participate in a specialist programme at that school
-- for that year; (b) to a child -- (i) who has a sibling who is enrolled at the school for that year other than a sibling who
-- is enrolled ... to participate in a specialist programme; and (ii) who lives nearest the school; (c) to [any other] child ...
-- who lives nearest the school." Within (b) and (c), the nearer child first.
-- Reg 15(1): for kindergarten (pre-compulsory) at a local-intake school: (a) in the intake area with a sibling enrolled; (b) in
-- the intake area without; (c) outside with a sibling; (d) outside without; within each, the nearest first.
@export From outside the intake area, in which priority group is my child (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 16)?
GIVEN `qualifies for a specialist programme there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child qualifies for a specialist programme at that school this year
      `a sibling enrolled there, other than in a specialist programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a brother or sister is enrolled there this year, other than to take part in a specialist programme
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my child's priority group from outside the intake area` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `qualifies for a specialist programme there` THEN 1
        IF `a sibling enrolled there, other than in a specialist programme` THEN 2
        OTHERWISE 3

@export For a kindergarten place at a local-intake school, in which priority group is my child (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `we live in its intake area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area
      `a sibling enrolled there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a brother or sister is enrolled there that year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my child's priority group for kindergarten` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `we live in its intake area` AND `a sibling enrolled there` THEN 1
        IF `we live in its intake area` THEN 2
        IF `a sibling enrolled there` THEN 3
        OTHERWISE 4

§§ `97, 98, 105, 106, regs 61-64 -- what the school may charge`

-- s 97: "first charges payment year in relation to a student -- (a) until 31 December 2010, means the first calendar year in
-- which the student had reached 12 years of age by the beginning of the year; and (b) on and from 1 January 2011 until 31
-- December 2014, ... 12 years and 6 months ...; and (c) on and from 1 January 2015, ... 11 years and 6 months by the beginning
-- of the year". Gloss: the year from which a government school may impose charges (s 98(3)); in practice Year 7 for a child
-- whose compulsory period began under s 6(1)(c). Each year is tested under the paragraph in force in it (INFERENCE).
GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has my child reached the charges age at the beginning of` IF
    BRANCH
        IF `the year` AT MOST 2010 THEN `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` `born on` 12 0 `the year`
        IF `the year` AT MOST 2014 THEN `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` `born on` 12 6 `the year`
        OTHERWISE `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` `born on` 11 6 `the year`

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first year from which my child is of charges age` MEANS
    IF `has my child reached the charges age at the beginning of` `born on` `from`
    THEN `from`
    ELSE `the first year from which my child is of charges age` `born on` (`from` PLUS 1)

@export Which is my child's first charges payment year (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 97)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my child's first charges payment year` MEANS
    `the first year from which my child is of charges age` `my child's date of birth` (DATE_YEAR `my child's date of birth` PLUS 10)

-- s 97: "adult student means a person who enrols at a government school in a year and whose compulsory education period has
-- ended before January in that year". "overseas student means a person who ... (a) is not entitled to reside permanently in
-- Australia; and (b) satisfies the criteria (if any) prescribed". Reg 62: the person "(a) is a Schedule 3A visa holder; or (b)
-- is not entitled under section 76 to be enrolled at a government school".
@export Is my child an adult student in this year (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 97)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child an adult student` IF
    Day (`the last day of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` (Date 1 1 `the year`)) LESS THAN Day (Date 1 1 `the year`)

@export Is my child an overseas student (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 97; reg 62)?
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child an overseas student` IF
        (NOT `the residence`'s `entitled to reside permanently in Australia`)
    AND (    elem (`the residence`'s `the visa subclass held`) `the Schedule 3A visa subclasses`
         OR  (NOT `Is my child qualified by residence` `the residence`))

-- s 98(1): "No fee for instruction may be imposed in respect of a student for the provision of -- (a) a nonoptional component
-- of an educational programme at a government school; or (b) an optional component ... if the instruction is provided by a
-- member of the teaching staff, unless the student is an overseas student or an adult student." (2): no contribution may be
-- sought towards such a fee.
DECLARE Component IS ONE OF
    `a non-optional component`
    `an optional component taught by the teaching staff`
    `an optional component taught by someone else`

@export May the government school charge a fee for instruction for my child (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 98(1))?
GIVEN `the component` IS A Component @desc What the instruction is for
      `an overseas student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is an overseas student
      `an adult student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is an adult student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the school charge a fee for instruction` IF
        `an overseas student`
    OR  `an adult student`
    OR  `the component` EQUALS `an optional component taught by someone else`

-- s 98(3): "No charge may be imposed ... for -- (a) materials provided in a nonoptional component ...; or (b) services or
-- facilities ... before the student's first charges payment year unless the student is an overseas student." (4): a
-- contribution (s 97: "voluntary contribution") may be sought instead.
-- Reg 61(1): "The maximum total amount of a contribution ... for materials referred to in regulation 59 and services referred to
-- in regulation 60(a) to (f) is $60.00 for each year in which the student -- (a) is in his or her pre-compulsory education
-- period; or (b) is in his or her compulsory education period before the student's first charges payment year."
-- (2): "The maximum total amount of a charge ... is $235.00 for -- (a) the student's first charges payment year; and (b) each
-- subsequent year until the end of the year in which the student reaches 15 years of age." (5): no contribution where a charge
-- has been determined. Reg 61 sets no limit outside those years (an overseas student before the first charges payment year;
-- any student after the year of turning 15): the answer says so.
DECLARE Limit IS ONE OF
    `at most` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `none may be imposed or sought`
    `no limit is prescribed by regulation 61`

`the most that may be sought as a contribution before charges begin` MEANS 60
`the most that may be charged from charges age to 15` MEANS 235

@export What is the most the government school can charge me this year for materials and services (s 98(3); reg 61(2))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
      `an overseas student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is an overseas student
GIVETH A Limit
`What is the most I can be charged for materials and services` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year` LESS THAN `my child's first charges payment year` `my child's date of birth`
            THEN IF `an overseas student` THEN `no limit is prescribed by regulation 61` ELSE `none may be imposed or sought`
        IF `the year` AT MOST `the year my child reaches` `my child's date of birth` 15 0
            THEN `at most` `the most that may be charged from charges age to 15`
        OTHERWISE `no limit is prescribed by regulation 61`

@export What is the most the government school can ask me to contribute this year for materials and services (s 98(4); reg 61(1), (5))?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
      `a charge has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the school has determined a charge for your child for the year
GIVETH A Limit
`What is the most I can be asked to contribute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a charge has been determined` THEN `none may be imposed or sought`
        IF `the year` LESS THAN `my child's first charges payment year` `my child's date of birth`
            THEN `at most` `the most that may be sought as a contribution before charges begin`
        OTHERWISE `no limit is prescribed by regulation 61`

-- Reg 61(3): for posting or telecommunicating materials to a School of Isolated and Distance Education student studying
-- outside Western Australia (reg 60(g)), a further maximum by region, "in addition to any other charge or contribution" (4).
DECLARE Region IS ONE OF
    `within Australia but outside Western Australia`
    `New Zealand`
    `the Pacific region other than New Zealand`
    `the South-East Asian region`
    `the Middle East and North America`
    `Europe and Russia, Africa, Central and South America`

@export What is the most the distance-education school can charge for sending materials to my child abroad (reg 61(3))?
GIVEN `the region` IS A Region @desc Where your child is studying
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for sending materials to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the region`
    WHEN `within Australia but outside Western Australia` THEN 130
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN 200
    WHEN `the Pacific region other than New Zealand` THEN 260
    WHEN `the South-East Asian region` THEN 300
    WHEN `the Middle East and North America` THEN 400
    WHEN `Europe and Russia, Africa, Central and South America` THEN 500

-- s 99(5): "All charges or contributions for a school year must be determined under subsection (3) and approved under
-- subsection (4) not later than 2 months before the beginning of the school year." (4): where the school has a Council, the
-- determination "does not have effect unless it has been approved by the Council". (7): a parent's not receiving the notice does
-- not affect validity.
@export Was this year's charge determined in time to have effect (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 99(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the school has a Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the school has a school Council
      `the Council approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Council approved the charge
      `determined and approved on` IS A DATE @desc The date by which the charge was determined and approved
      `the school year begins on` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the school year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the charge determined in time` IF
        ((NOT `the school has a Council`) OR `the Council approved it`)
    AND Day (Date (DATE_DAY `determined and approved on`) (DATE_MONTH `determined and approved on` PLUS 2) (DATE_YEAR `determined and approved on`))
        AT MOST Day `the school year begins on`

-- s 105: "A principal of a government school must not exclude a student, other than an overseas student or an adult student,
-- from participating in an educational programme of the school for the nonpayment of a charge payable under section 99."
@export Can my child be kept out of classes because I have not paid the charges (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 105)?
GIVEN `an overseas student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is an overseas student
      `an adult student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is an adult student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my child be excluded for unpaid charges` IF `an overseas student` OR `an adult student`

-- s 106(1): a fee or charge "may be recovered as a debt ... (a) from a parent of the student; or (b) in the case of a student
-- who has turned 18 or who is a prescribed child, from the student". (2): before "any administrative or legal action", the
-- chief executive officer is to ensure "(a) inquiries have been made into the reasons for the failure to pay ...; and (b) all
-- reasonably practicable steps have been taken to recover ...; and (c) the circumstances of the person ... and the person's
-- capacity to pay have been taken into account". "Parent" is defined only "in relation to a child" (s 4), so (INFERENCE) the
-- parent route is open only while the student is under 18.
@export Can unpaid school charges be recovered from me as a debt (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 106)?
GIVEN `my child is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is under 18
      `the reasons were inquired into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether inquiries were made into why the charge was not paid
      `every practicable step was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all reasonably practicable steps were taken to recover it
      `my circumstances were considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your circumstances and capacity to pay were taken into account
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the charges be recovered from me` IF
        `my child is under 18`
    AND `the reasons were inquired into`
    AND `every practicable step was taken`
    AND `my circumstances were considered`

-- s 103: overseas and adult students "pay such fees for instruction as may be prescribed". Reg 63(1): "The maximum total amount
-- of the fees for instruction ... is $25 000 each school year." Reg 64(2): no fee is payable by an adult student enrolled for
-- 2014 or later if "(a) [enrolled] in an educational programme that is based on the learning outcomes set out in the outline of
-- curriculum and assessment; and (b) the student does not reach the age of 19 years and 6 months by 1 January of the year";
-- reg 64(1): for 2013 or earlier, "19 years". The waivers in regs 65 and 66 are the chief executive officer's: not encoded.
@export What is the most a government school can charge in fees for instruction in a year (reg 63(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a fee for instruction can be` MEANS 25000

@export As an adult student, is my child exempt from fees for instruction (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 64)?
GIVEN `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year your child is enrolled for
      `a curriculum-based programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programme is based on the learning outcomes in the outline of curriculum and assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my adult child exempt from fees for instruction` IF
        `a curriculum-based programme`
    AND (NOT `reached the age`)
    WHERE
        `reached the age` MEANS
            IF `the year` AT MOST 2013
            THEN `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` `my child's date of birth` 19 0 `the year`
            ELSE `had my child reached the age by the beginning of` `my child's date of birth` 19 6 `the year`
